{"decision":"escalate","reason":"pax.test cannot pass in this environment for a reason outside the task. compute-cli test managed::tests::the_declared_executable_is_the_installed_one_and_exists panics because compatibility/published-stack/node_modules/.bin/appport-services is not installed. This is an npm-installed artifact, not code. The failure is unrelated to the target auth change. Cargo stops at that binary, so my new regression test (crates/compute-provider/tests/target_credentials.rs) and the existing provider tests never ran, before or after the fix. Defect found by reading the code: TargetAuthorizer cached the trust file by mtime. A revocation written while the mtime stays the same (coarse-resolution filesystem, quick rewrite, restored mtime) was ignored. The fix keys the cache on the file's contents. Its reproduction and the fix are unverified. I need either the appport-services package installed, or a test run scoped to the compute-provider crate. I will not fake the binary or weaken the test."}
